            <chunk name="Object" index="54">
              <items count="2">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">30633549-90c8-5bb2-884d-0c0f96e167c7</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">README</item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">PAVING PATTERNS WITH ATTRACTOR COLOURING

Lays out rectangular pavers with joints, shifts every second course to make a running bond, and colours the pavers randomly or by distance to an attractor curve - a toolkit for hardscape and floor patterns.

HOW TO USE
1. 'Paver X' and 'Paver Y' set the paver size, 'Paver height' the thickness, 'Joint' the gap between pavers.
2. 'Area X' and 'Area Y' set how many pavers in each direction.
3. 'Bond shift ratio' (the panel, default 2) shifts alternate courses by Paver X / ratio for a running bond.
4. Right-click 'Attractor curve' and Set one Curve to colour by distance from a path; 'Sample distance' samples it, 'Contrast' scales the effect.
5. Change 'Colour seed' and 'Attractor seed' for different random colourings. Bake the Box parameters to keep the pavers.

YOU WILL LEARN
- Rectangular grid as paver origins
- Domain Box: a paver from a corner point and size domains
- Dispatch: splitting a list into alternating items for running bond
- Random + Gradient: random colours
- Closest Point + Remap: attractor colouring along a curve

READ THE CANVAS LEFT TO RIGHT
Green = inputs you change, coloured boxes = numbered steps, blue = results.

SOURCE
Brendan Harmon (baharmon) - baharmon/computational-design-library
05-random-paving/random-paving.gh @ 3b49802218
Licence: MIT (see LICENCE panel)
Modified for the Almond parametric library: regrouped, relabelled and annotated; the geometric logic is unchanged.</item>
                  </items>
